From 8e9a5f58c0dc458d22e8720b31c1a0cb76e7ecd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mi210 <mi210@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:49:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] hip: Inkling-2 decode fusions round 1 (clip, SITU, MoE
 down tail, loop control)

Backend-level pattern fusions for the node chains emitted by
src/models/inkling2.cpp; each reproduces the original kernels arithmetic
(reduction trees, contraction) so decode logits stay bit-identical.
- clip: [mul] sqr sum_rows sqrt scale fill div clamp mul -> 1 kernel
- situ: scale tanh scale sigmoid mul scale tanh scale mul -> 1 kernel
- moe_down: repeat get_rows + weighted expert sum -> 1 kernel
- ctrl_norm: concat + rms_norm -> 1 kernel
- ctrl_gate: forget/gain K=64 GEMVs + tanh/scale/mul/add -> 1 kernel
Switches GGML_CUDA_INK_{FUSE,CLIP,SITU,MOE_DOWN,CTRL_NORM,CTRL_GATE}=0,
stats GGML_CUDA_FUSION_STATS=1, node dump GGML_CUDA_DUMP_NODES=<file>,
bit-compare debug GGML_CUDA_INK_VERIFY=1 (with graphs disabled).
tg128 33.0 -> 39.7 tok/s; kld.sh -ub 1 logits md5 identical to baseline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
